---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Damien Herlihy"
  description="What this site collects (an email address if you subscribe, nothing else you don't type), the cookieless analytics it runs, and how to be forgotten."
>
  <article class="privacy">
    <p class="privacy-kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>The short, honest version</h1>
    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated 6 August 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Who runs this</h2>
      <p>Damien Herlihy. Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:damienmunchip@gmail.com">damienmunchip@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>Your <strong>email address</strong> — only if you type it into the newsletter form. It goes to <strong>Audienceful</strong>, the service that sends the newsletter, and nowhere else.</p>
      <p>One footnote: the newsletter form's script comes from Audienceful's CDN, and its bot protection (Cloudflare) sets one short-lived cookie (<code>__cf_bm</code>, about 30 minutes) on Audienceful's own domain. It tells humans from bots; it doesn't track you across sites.</p>
      <p>The contact form doesn't send anything to a server at all — it opens your own email app with a pre-filled draft, and nothing leaves your machine until you press send.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Analytics, without the creepy part</h2>
      <p>The site uses <strong>PostHog</strong>, running on EU servers, to count page views and a few clicks (like which essays get read). It's configured cookieless: nothing is stored in your browser, no session recording, no automatic click-tracking, no identity across visits. If you come back tomorrow, it doesn't know you're you.</p>
      <p>No advertising cookies, no cross-site tracking, no selling data — ever.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>Typefaces load from Google Fonts, so that request reaches a Google server — which, like any web request, sees your IP address. No cookies are involved.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How long, and how to leave</h2>
      <p>Your email stays on the newsletter list until you unsubscribe — there's a link in every email. Want it deleted entirely? Email me and it's gone.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 72px 24px 64px;
  }

  .privacy-kicker {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .privacy h1 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .privacy-updated {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .privacy section {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 17px;
  }

  .privacy p {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .privacy a {
    color: var(--gold-bright);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
